  </data>
  <data name="Calculator_HowItWorks_Budget" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Both income and expenses for future months come straight from the selected budget's per-category monthly amounts. The split percentages below describe how expenses would be apportioned across income sources — they don't change the projection in this mode.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Calculator_HowItWorks_Recent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Each income category's last completed calendar month is repeated flat across the remaining months. "Projected Yearly" = past actuals + last-month income × remaining months. Use this to see whether current income covers the rest of the year's budgeted expenses.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Calculator_HowItWorks_Breakeven" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Each row's split percentage determines what share of the year's projected expenses that income source needs to cover. "Required" = total expenses × split. "Remaining" = the source's income minus what it owes. Edit the splits to model different ways to divide responsibility; Save persists them on the selected budget.</value>
  </data>
